        question: "Why can't retail and apartments share an air handler?",
        answer: "Because their schedules, loads, and ventilation needs are incompatible. Retail needs high cooling and ventilation during business hours with frequent door openings; apartments need quiet, steady, individually controlled comfort around the clock with continuous low-level ventilation. A shared air handler forces one schedule on both — the apartments get retail's noise and the retail gets the apartments' setback — and shared ductwork risks carrying odors and, in a fire, smoke between the occupancies.",
